DrawingML: export supplemental script fonts from the theme model

Theme import already populates both FontScheme supplemental lists.
ThemeExport wrote only latin/ea/cs and dropped every a:font mapping.
Write both model lists after the primary fonts in each collection.
This preserves script-specific major/minor choices, including edits,
without restoring original theme XML over the current document model.

The regression covers eight scripts with different major/minor fonts,
checks all sixteen mappings and the body after two DOCX saves.
A rebuilt C++ engine must still run this regression before release.

diff --git a/oox/source/export/ThemeExport.cxx b/oox/source/export/ThemeExport.cxx
--- a/oox/source/export/ThemeExport.cxx
+++ b/oox/source/export/ThemeExport.cxx
@@ -124,6 +124,10 @@
         mpFS->singleElementNS(XML_a, XML_cs, aAttrList);
     }
 
+    for (auto const& rFont : rFontScheme.getMajorSupplementalFontList())
+        mpFS->singleElementNS(XML_a, XML_font, XML_script, rFont.maScript,
+                             XML_typeface, rFont.maTypeface);
+
     mpFS->endElementNS(XML_a, XML_majorFont);
 
     mpFS->startElementNS(XML_a, XML_minorFont);
@@ -143,6 +147,10 @@
         fillAttrList(aAttrList, rFontScheme.getMinorComplex());
         mpFS->singleElementNS(XML_a, XML_cs, aAttrList);
     }
+
+    for (auto const& rFont : rFontScheme.getMinorSupplementalFontList())
+        mpFS->singleElementNS(XML_a, XML_font, XML_script, rFont.maScript,
+                             XML_typeface, rFont.maTypeface);
 
     mpFS->endElementNS(XML_a, XML_minorFont);
 
